WEBVTT

1
00:00:47.672 --> 00:00:50.967
THE APARTMENT JOB

2
00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:59.059
Mr. Park. I'm sorry.
but I can't work here anymore.

3
00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.895
You can't just quit like this.

4
00:01:01.978 --> 00:01:03.855
You fired me suddenly too.

5
00:01:03.938 --> 00:01:06.441
You already received your payment.
You should do your job.

6
00:01:06.524 --> 00:01:08.651
What's the point in being your wife
for two more weeks?

7
00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:11.946
You already got the position
that you wanted so badly.

8
00:01:12.947 --> 00:01:15.742
Our family still needs you. Ms. Kang.

9
00:01:15.825 --> 00:01:19.746
Mr. Park. that family you speak of
is fake anyway!

10
00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:21.623
What?

11
00:01:22.665 --> 00:01:23.666
"Fake"?

12
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.627
Oh. my goodness. You…

13
00:01:26.961 --> 00:01:29.088
So you guys…

14
00:01:30.006 --> 00:01:31.508
were a fake family?

15
00:01:32.884 --> 00:01:34.177
I see.

16
00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.263
My gosh. I get it now.

17
00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:39.724
I did think it was strange.

18
00:01:39.808 --> 00:01:43.061
Those guys were telling their father
they'd cut off his hands.

19
00:01:43.144 --> 00:01:45.355
and you were telling the boy
to call you Ha-ri.

20
00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:48.066
I was wondering
what kind of messed-up family you were.

21
00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:49.901
So that's why.

22
00:01:50.652 --> 00:01:53.571
Everything was fake.

23
00:01:54.489 --> 00:01:55.490
Fake?

24
00:01:55.573 --> 00:01:56.866
You misheard.

25
00:01:58.326 --> 00:01:59.702
I said. "Take."

26
00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:02.747
I told her we needed to
take it easy on the salt.

27
00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:05.583
Right. honey.

28
00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.252
The kimchi stew was pretty salty.

29
00:02:07.335 --> 00:02:09.087
-It was salty.
-Yeah. it was.

30
00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:10.421
It was salty.

31
00:02:10.505 --> 00:02:11.464
Enough about the stew.

32
00:02:11.548 --> 00:02:14.717
I heard it clearly with my own ears.

33
00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.345
"That family you speak of is fake anyway!"

34
00:02:17.428 --> 00:02:19.305
You misheard!

35
00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:20.974
That's nonsense.

36
00:02:21.057 --> 00:02:23.226
-Why would we fake a family?
-Right.

37
00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.602
Why would you do that?

38
00:02:24.686 --> 00:02:27.522
But you should know
that this is a serious matter.

39
00:02:27.605 --> 00:02:30.692
You've deceived
this entire apartment complex.

40
00:02:30.775 --> 00:02:31.985
you understand?

41
00:02:32.068 --> 00:02:33.486
Ms. Jang. that's not--

42
00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:34.404
But…

43
00:02:35.196 --> 00:02:37.073
why did you go to such lengths

44
00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:39.117
to become the president?

45
00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.077
What are you scheming?

46
00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.453
What are you up to?

47
00:02:42.537 --> 00:02:43.872
-No. wait. Forget it.
-Ms. Jang…

48
00:02:43.955 --> 00:02:45.999
President Park… I mean. Mr. Park.

49
00:02:46.082 --> 00:02:47.458
You…

50
00:02:48.042 --> 00:02:49.878
should step down immediately.

51
00:02:50.378 --> 00:02:53.923
I can't just let this slide.

52
00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:56.593
I'm going to post this
on our community forum.

53
00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:59.262
-Move aside.
-It's under maintenance.

54
00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:02.932
Darn it. This stupid elevator
is always out of order.

55
00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.559
You frauds.

56
00:03:05.226 --> 00:03:07.312
Ms. Jang…

57
00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:23.995
Emergency!

58
00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:27.081
Ms. Jang just found out
that we're a fake family.

59
00:03:27.165 --> 00:03:28.166
What?

60
00:03:29.959 --> 00:03:32.045
She just said
she's going to post this online.

61
00:03:32.128 --> 00:03:33.546
We have to stop her.

62
00:03:37.675 --> 00:03:39.052
What's going on?

63
00:03:39.677 --> 00:03:43.223
Why isn't the internet working?

64
00:03:43.306 --> 00:03:45.683
What's wrong with this apartment?

65
00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:47.852
And why is the elevator

66
00:03:47.936 --> 00:03:49.479
stuck on the 29th floor?

67
00:03:52.774 --> 00:03:54.859
I can't hold on any longer.

68
00:03:57.779 --> 00:03:58.780
Gosh.

69
00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.324
What?

70
00:04:02.116 --> 00:04:03.576
I'm sorry. ma'am.

71
00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.662
It's not opening. Geez.

72
00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:06.746
What's going on?

73
00:04:07.497 --> 00:04:08.414
Darn it!

74
00:04:08.498 --> 00:04:10.124
This stupid apartment!

75
00:04:10.208 --> 00:04:12.377
I've had it with this place!

76
00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:23.846
{\an8}It must smell nice
because it's from France.

77
00:04:24.806 --> 00:04:26.474
{\an8}It's my first time using hand lotion.

78
00:04:27.058 --> 00:04:28.643
{\an8}You didn't need to get me a gift.

79
00:04:29.227 --> 00:04:30.937
{\an8}It's a farewell gift. Mr. Choi.

80
00:04:34.023 --> 00:04:36.859
{\an8}You scare me whenever you say that.

81
00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:38.695
{\an8}I told you several times.

82
00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:40.363
{\an8}And President Seo

83
00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:43.491
{\an8}also asked me to continue
just until the end of his term.

84
00:04:44.075 --> 00:04:46.494
{\an8}So you returned when you heard
the president had changed?

85
00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:48.204
{\an8}Yes.

86
00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.083
President Seo

87
00:04:52.166 --> 00:04:54.711
is in a tight spot
because he lost the election.

88
00:04:56.045 --> 00:04:59.340
None of us expected him
to lose that position.

89
00:05:00.675 --> 00:05:02.218
I'll talk to him

90
00:05:02.927 --> 00:05:05.805
when the timing is right.

91
00:05:05.888 --> 00:05:07.807
so please stay until then.

92
00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:11.894
Without you here. our apartment complex
will be in huge trouble.

93
00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:22.071
Ha-jeong.

94
00:05:22.864 --> 00:05:24.407
It was a misunderstanding earlier.

95
00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.160
Our company's client asked me
to look after their son.

96
00:05:29.954 --> 00:05:33.207
Why would a lawyer
visit a client's house to do such work?

97
00:05:33.708 --> 00:05:35.376
And he called you "Mom."

98
00:05:36.461 --> 00:05:38.046
I had no choice. I'm just a newbie.

99
00:05:38.129 --> 00:05:39.630
I have to do as I'm told.

100
00:05:40.214 --> 00:05:42.425
And he loves me more than his mom.

101
00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:44.218
He just calls me "Mom" sometimes.

102
00:05:53.061 --> 00:05:55.104
You studied hard to become a lawyer.

103
00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:57.857
It upsets me
to see you running errands like that.

104
00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:00.276
Well. I told them I can't do it anymore.

105
00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:05.448
But why did you return so early?
Your trip was supposed to last longer.

106
00:06:07.283 --> 00:06:09.702
Something came up at work.

107
00:06:11.245 --> 00:06:14.290
You should've told me
so I could be prepared.

108
00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:16.000
Prepared for what?

109
00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:22.006
I mean. I would've picked you up
from the airport.

110
00:06:22.924 --> 00:06:24.717
Give me that. It must be heavy.

111
00:06:25.468 --> 00:06:26.511
How was France?

112
00:06:27.095 --> 00:06:30.139
It was nice. but I did miss spicy food.

113
00:06:31.057 --> 00:06:35.019
That's a tacky way
to flaunt that you were abroad.

114
00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:40.733
You remember. right?

115
00:06:42.819 --> 00:06:45.154
<i>First encounter. library</i>
<i>First kiss. under a street light</i>

116
00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:46.781
<i>Fateful encounter</i>
<i>At a book club after-party</i>

117
00:06:48.658 --> 00:06:52.328
We checked that Ms. Jang went home
after struggling with the door last night.

118
00:06:52.411 --> 00:06:54.580
She'll come out
for her morning exercise soon.

119
00:06:54.664 --> 00:06:55.498
Okay. got it.

120
00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:59.460
Since it's an emergency.
I'll allow a wide range of touching.

121
00:07:03.422 --> 00:07:05.174
She's coming.

122
00:07:07.051 --> 00:07:08.177
Honey. hurry up.

123
00:07:09.387 --> 00:07:11.013
Careful not to get hurt. honey.

124
00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:13.516
You can protect me.

125
00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:15.601
I do protect you. don't I?

126
00:07:16.185 --> 00:07:17.270
-Shall we go?
-Yes.

127
00:07:17.854 --> 00:07:19.063
Gosh.

128
00:07:19.147 --> 00:07:20.898
I can tell that you're faking it.

129
00:07:20.982 --> 00:07:22.525
It's so obvious.

130
00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:24.610
Married couples
don't run around holding hands.

131
00:07:25.528 --> 00:07:27.613
Geez.

132
00:07:27.697 --> 00:07:29.532
We used to be in a book club.

133
00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:32.243
I fell in love with her at first sight
at a library.

134
00:07:32.326 --> 00:07:33.786
Our first kiss was under a street light.

135
00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:35.037
Our first kiss…

136
00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:38.374
I don't want to know.
I'm not curious at all.

137
00:07:38.458 --> 00:07:40.585
I don't want to hear it!

138
00:07:41.252 --> 00:07:42.336
-Ms. Jang!
-Ms. Jang!

139
00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:50.428
One week.

140
00:07:51.053 --> 00:07:53.598
Can't you just wait one week?

141
00:07:55.683 --> 00:07:56.809
One week?

142
00:07:57.518 --> 00:08:00.438
What are you planning to do
during that week?

143
00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:05.276
Can't you give me a chance
to win back your trust?

144
00:08:10.072 --> 00:08:11.282
Don't you remember this place?

145
00:08:11.365 --> 00:08:13.034
Cut!

146
00:08:13.117 --> 00:08:14.577
That was soulless.

147
00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:16.037
Why is your tone so cold?

148
00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:18.539
You need to express more sincerity. Again!

149
00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:20.625
Sincerity.

150
00:08:21.918 --> 00:08:23.085
Do you remember this place?

151
00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:25.379
You and I stood here together

152
00:08:25.463 --> 00:08:28.299
and shouted ourselves hoarse
for a common goal.

153
00:08:28.883 --> 00:08:32.094
That glorious memory
of our struggle paying off

154
00:08:32.178 --> 00:08:34.597
is still engraved deep in my heart.

155
00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:36.849
All right. fine.

156
00:08:36.933 --> 00:08:38.726
That was a happy memory for me too.

157
00:08:38.809 --> 00:08:40.520
Our housing prices rose thanks to that.

158
00:08:40.603 --> 00:08:42.730
I do admire you for it.

159
00:08:42.813 --> 00:08:44.190
But you must have

160
00:08:44.273 --> 00:08:46.567
some reason to fake a family

161
00:08:46.651 --> 00:08:48.945
to become the president…

162
00:08:49.028 --> 00:08:50.196
…of the residents' association!

163
00:08:50.279 --> 00:08:52.406
I'm telling you. we're not a fake family.

164
00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:53.991
I really…

165
00:08:57.954 --> 00:08:58.996
love my wife.

166
00:09:00.289 --> 00:09:02.208
Sure. you do.

167
00:09:02.291 --> 00:09:03.918
You have to sincerely believe it

168
00:09:04.001 --> 00:09:06.921
when you say you love your wife. Again!

169
00:09:07.004 --> 00:09:07.880
Right.

170
00:09:08.589 --> 00:09:10.591
I really love my wife.

171
00:09:11.676 --> 00:09:12.593
I love her!

172
00:09:12.677 --> 00:09:13.970
I love her!

173
00:09:14.053 --> 00:09:15.555
I love her! With gestures too!

174
00:09:15.638 --> 00:09:17.139
-I love her!
-I love her!

175
00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:18.641
Gestures! I love her!

176
00:09:18.724 --> 00:09:22.061
I love her!

177
00:09:29.318 --> 00:09:30.987
I love my wife.

178
00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:33.781
I married her because I love her.
and we even had a child.

179
00:09:33.864 --> 00:09:36.158
I didn't want to tell you this.

180
00:09:36.242 --> 00:09:38.744
but my brothers
all have different mothers.

181
00:09:38.828 --> 00:09:41.080
Gosh. All three of them?

182
00:09:41.872 --> 00:09:44.917
My father had
a rather scandalous life in his youth.

183
00:09:45.001 --> 00:09:46.961
Right. I did think it was strange.

184
00:09:47.044 --> 00:09:51.299
You didn't look anything alike.

185
00:09:51.382 --> 00:09:52.758
What's more…

186
00:09:53.384 --> 00:09:55.553
my father started gambling. so…

187
00:09:55.636 --> 00:09:56.721
Oh. dear.

188
00:09:56.804 --> 00:09:58.347
We were so scarred because of him.

189
00:09:58.431 --> 00:10:02.310
but we were living together
to mend our relationship.

190
00:10:02.393 --> 00:10:05.605
Right. I see.

191
00:10:05.688 --> 00:10:07.273
-Oh. dear.
-Nice.

192
00:10:10.151 --> 00:10:12.069
Fine. let's say that's true.

193
00:10:12.695 --> 00:10:13.863
However…

194
00:10:14.363 --> 00:10:17.783
from all the data I've collected so far.

195
00:10:17.867 --> 00:10:20.202
you guys are very suspicious.

196
00:10:20.286 --> 00:10:23.623
I have a bad feeling about you.

197
00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:28.836
That's why I'm asking you
to make your judgment after one week.

198
00:10:28.919 --> 00:10:31.422
It won't be too late to decide then.

199
00:10:37.428 --> 00:10:38.929
I didn't want to bring this up.

200
00:10:39.597 --> 00:10:43.142
but the maintenance fees
you're always complaining about…

201
00:10:46.145 --> 00:10:47.313
What?

202
00:10:47.396 --> 00:10:49.565
What about the maintenance fees?

203
00:10:50.941 --> 00:10:53.027
I think there's an issue with them.

204
00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:55.821
To be honest. I was investigating it.

205
00:10:56.697 --> 00:10:59.325
You were investigating that matter?

206
00:10:59.408 --> 00:11:01.118
You should've told me.

207
00:11:01.202 --> 00:11:02.787
So that's what you were doing.

208
00:11:06.499 --> 00:11:09.001
All right. fine.

209
00:11:10.544 --> 00:11:13.005
Then I'll give you just one week.
That's it.

210
00:11:13.506 --> 00:11:14.924
One week.

211
00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:23.974
THE APARTMENT JOB

212
00:11:24.767 --> 00:11:25.601
Boss.

213
00:11:26.769 --> 00:11:28.020
How did it go?

214
00:11:28.729 --> 00:11:31.315
We have one more week.

215
00:11:32.274 --> 00:11:34.735
We have to find the fund
within a week and flee.

216
00:11:35.945 --> 00:11:38.114
The Lizard. Bring him here.

217
00:11:38.197 --> 00:11:40.616
-Right.
-Lizard.

218
00:11:42.827 --> 00:11:44.495
I've been thinking about it.

219
00:11:45.246 --> 00:11:46.247
And?

220
00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:49.417
I've racked my brains.

221
00:11:50.042 --> 00:11:52.711
but let's say the facility manager.
the accounting manager.

222
00:11:52.795 --> 00:11:55.589
and the president teamed up
and pocketed the fund.

223
00:11:55.673 --> 00:11:57.174
But even so.

224
00:11:57.258 --> 00:12:00.177
they wouldn't have emptied out
the entire account like this.

225
00:12:00.261 --> 00:12:02.972
You've been the president for a few days.
so you'd know.

226
00:12:03.055 --> 00:12:07.435
Apartment complexes
have fixed monthly expenses.

227
00:12:07.518 --> 00:12:09.645
and unexpected emergency costs
come up all the time.

228
00:12:09.728 --> 00:12:11.480
Emptying out the entire account

229
00:12:11.564 --> 00:12:13.774
makes no sense.

230
00:12:13.858 --> 00:12:14.984
What's your point?

231
00:12:16.819 --> 00:12:20.030
There must be someone behind this.

232
00:12:20.823 --> 00:12:21.991
What?

233
00:12:22.074 --> 00:12:25.327
There are three major methods
to pocket the fund.

234
00:12:25.411 --> 00:12:27.621
First is to manipulate the books

235
00:12:27.705 --> 00:12:30.374
and skim off a little at a time.

236
00:12:30.458 --> 00:12:34.044
The second is to inflate
the construction costs. pay it out.

237
00:12:34.128 --> 00:12:35.963
then get a kickback from the contractor.

238
00:12:36.046 --> 00:12:39.133
Then the third is to just say.
"Screw it" and spend the money.

239
00:12:39.717 --> 00:12:41.051
Which method did you use?

240
00:12:41.135 --> 00:12:45.139
I mixed all three methods. of course.

241
00:12:45.222 --> 00:12:46.974
Anyway. none of these methods

242
00:12:47.057 --> 00:12:49.435
would result
in an entirely empty bank account.

243
00:12:49.518 --> 00:12:52.646
Why? There can't be any problems
with emergency spending

244
00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:55.024
for you to pocket the money
without getting caught.

245
00:12:55.107 --> 00:12:58.402
That means someone powerful
is backing them.

246
00:12:59.487 --> 00:13:02.656
So there's someone behind the scenes
controlling the reserve fund?

247
00:13:04.575 --> 00:13:05.618
Who?

248
00:13:08.579 --> 00:13:09.788
How would I know?

249
00:13:10.623 --> 00:13:12.041
-Bring the bag.
-It's in my closet.

250
00:13:12.124 --> 00:13:14.001
-Should we go up to the roof again?
-Wait.

251
00:13:14.084 --> 00:13:15.169
It might help you think.

252
00:13:15.252 --> 00:13:16.670
There's a way to find out.

253
00:13:21.592 --> 00:13:25.012
Use the fund with your position.

254
00:13:25.095 --> 00:13:27.014
Whether it's construction or whatever.

255
00:13:27.097 --> 00:13:29.183
make something up
that requires you to use the fund.

256
00:13:29.266 --> 00:13:31.685
But if the construction proceeds

257
00:13:31.769 --> 00:13:33.812
when the account is empty.

258
00:13:33.896 --> 00:13:36.440
that means the money was paid

259
00:13:36.524 --> 00:13:38.943
and someone paid the contractor.

260
00:13:39.026 --> 00:13:42.696
It would cost quite a lot.
Will there be any issues using the fund?

261
00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:44.615
Not at all.

262
00:13:44.698 --> 00:13:46.784
This is exactly what
the reserve fund is for.

263
00:13:50.371 --> 00:13:51.497
We don't have time.

264
00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:54.833
Find anything that can be paid for
out of the reserve fund.

265
00:13:55.793 --> 00:13:56.710
-Yes. Boss!
-Yes. Boss!

266
00:13:59.421 --> 00:14:01.715
<i>Don't let a single tile or nail</i>
<i>go unchecked.</i>

267
00:14:01.799 --> 00:14:03.342
<i>Check things that look fine too.</i>

268
00:14:03.842 --> 00:14:05.135
<i>Starting tomorrow.</i>

269
00:14:05.219 --> 00:14:07.680
<i>we're making sure this place</i>
<i>is under constant construction.</i>

270
00:14:07.763 --> 00:14:09.431
-Let's find…
-Defects!

271
00:14:13.227 --> 00:14:14.186
Let's find some…

272
00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:16.438
The drains are way too open.

273
00:14:17.064 --> 00:14:18.482
They need to be open!

274
00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:22.570
Over here.

275
00:14:22.653 --> 00:14:24.446
We can do crack repairs here.

276
00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:26.365
See? I told you there were a lot.

277
00:14:27.157 --> 00:14:28.909
-There's one here!
-There's one here too!

278
00:14:30.035 --> 00:14:31.370
I found one here too.

279
00:14:33.747 --> 00:14:34.707
That's a selfie.

280
00:14:40.754 --> 00:14:41.714
It's leaking!

281
00:14:47.177 --> 00:14:48.220
A leak repair.

282
00:15:00.024 --> 00:15:02.526
Lizard. this one's a different color.
What's with this?

283
00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:04.111
It's the design.

284
00:15:05.112 --> 00:15:07.615
-What is it?
-I just tripped on a block. Right here.

285
00:15:08.949 --> 00:15:10.200
Hello.

286
00:15:10.284 --> 00:15:12.828
The new president is working really hard.

287
00:15:12.912 --> 00:15:14.121
Yeah. I'm glad he got elected.

288
00:15:14.204 --> 00:15:16.498
-Yeah. He's doing a great job.
-He is.

289
00:15:20.419 --> 00:15:21.670
Why is he working so hard?

290
00:15:25.591 --> 00:15:26.675
Great job. everyone.

291
00:15:26.759 --> 00:15:28.260
Let's enjoy our lunch.

292
00:15:28.344 --> 00:15:29.219
-Yes. sir.
-Yes. sir.

293
00:15:29.303 --> 00:15:31.263
You put all of these in?

294
00:15:31.347 --> 00:15:32.765
How do you make a profit?

295
00:15:32.848 --> 00:15:36.185
I want an Italian BMT sandwich
on grain bread.

296
00:15:36.268 --> 00:15:37.937
creamy egg salad with extra avocado.

297
00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:39.438
meat. pepperoni. and cheese.

298
00:15:39.521 --> 00:15:41.106
For the sauce. sweet low-sugar onion.

299
00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:43.150
tangy red wine vinegar
and a sprinkle of salt.

300
00:15:44.151 --> 00:15:46.153
-What will you have?
-Just have one.

301
00:15:46.236 --> 00:15:47.613
It's one sandwich.

302
00:15:47.696 --> 00:15:48.656
Really?

303
00:15:48.739 --> 00:15:51.200
I want one with meat.

304
00:15:51.283 --> 00:15:53.160
Stop. We'll all order the same one.

305
00:15:53.869 --> 00:15:55.746
Steak and cheese. please.

306
00:15:58.958 --> 00:16:00.709
This is really tasty.

307
00:16:00.793 --> 00:16:02.294
What is this? It's so good.

308
00:16:02.378 --> 00:16:04.755
This will keep me full until dinner.

309
00:16:04.838 --> 00:16:07.508
This is perfect for a man my age too.

310
00:16:08.217 --> 00:16:11.762
We did find things
to spend the reserve fund on.

311
00:16:11.845 --> 00:16:13.597
but what do we do now. Mr. Park?

312
00:16:13.681 --> 00:16:15.099
We need to move.

313
00:16:15.182 --> 00:16:16.016
FACILITY MANAGER

314
00:16:19.228 --> 00:16:21.855
Mr. Choi. we need
a building rep meeting immediately.

315
00:16:22.606 --> 00:16:24.566
Our apartment complex is a mess.

316
00:16:25.234 --> 00:16:27.695
Let's tackle the issues one by one.

317
00:16:27.778 --> 00:16:29.697
{\an8}EMERGENCY MEETING
ORGANIZER: PARK HAE-KANG

318
00:16:38.872 --> 00:16:39.999
All right.

319
00:16:43.168 --> 00:16:44.336
Hello.

320
00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:46.797
I'm President Park Hae-kang of True Value.

321
00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:55.681
I called this emergency meeting today

322
00:16:55.764 --> 00:16:58.308
because there are several
urgent matters to address.

323
00:16:58.392 --> 00:17:00.978
It's been about six years
since residents moved in.

324
00:17:01.061 --> 00:17:03.564
so we're starting to see problems
popping up here and there.

325
00:17:03.647 --> 00:17:04.815
So first.

326
00:17:04.898 --> 00:17:08.527
I'd like to repair
the cracks in the parking lot.

327
00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:11.905
This must be done
with the long-term repair reserve fund.

328
00:17:12.823 --> 00:17:14.324
Excuse me.

329
00:17:14.408 --> 00:17:16.744
The parking lot floor is completely fine.

330
00:17:17.536 --> 00:17:20.289
You might not know
since you're new to the job.

331
00:17:20.372 --> 00:17:23.584
but you can't just use the fund
recklessly like that.

332
00:17:25.044 --> 00:17:26.879
I'm not suggesting we use it recklessly.

333
00:17:26.962 --> 00:17:29.048
I've been told we can use
the reserve fund for this

334
00:17:29.131 --> 00:17:31.592
since it's for facility replacement
and repairs.

335
00:17:31.675 --> 00:17:33.594
Just because it's possible

336
00:17:33.677 --> 00:17:37.264
doesn't mean this repair is necessary.

337
00:17:37.347 --> 00:17:38.807
Are you saying

338
00:17:38.891 --> 00:17:42.644
that we can just tear apart
or replace things that are perfectly fine

339
00:17:42.728 --> 00:17:44.772
as long as the fund covers it?

340
00:17:45.981 --> 00:17:48.233
I checked the apartment complex
here and there.

341
00:17:48.317 --> 00:17:50.027
and it wasn't perfectly fine.

342
00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:52.071
There are chips and scrapes everywhere.

343
00:17:52.154 --> 00:17:53.781
Construction is absolutely necessary.

344
00:17:55.032 --> 00:17:57.076
We should hold off as long as we can.

345
00:17:57.159 --> 00:17:59.369
You shouldn't waste
the reserve fund like this.

346
00:17:59.453 --> 00:18:00.454
Waste?

347
00:18:00.537 --> 00:18:03.082
It's his first time as president.

348
00:18:03.165 --> 00:18:05.834
He's just clueless about his job.

349
00:18:08.045 --> 00:18:10.798
Then let's put this to a vote.

350
00:18:10.881 --> 00:18:14.426
Who here agrees to repairing the cracks

351
00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:15.594
in the parking lot?

352
00:18:22.309 --> 00:18:24.103
All right. Those who oppose?

353
00:18:29.358 --> 00:18:30.943
The second item on the agenda

354
00:18:31.026 --> 00:18:33.195
is repairing the leak in the machine room.

355
00:18:33.278 --> 00:18:35.948
<i>Who agrees to using the reserve fund?</i>

356
00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:37.699
<i>Who opposes?</i>

357
00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:41.286
What? Everyone's opposing.

358
00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:44.123
And replacing the pavement blocks.

359
00:18:44.206 --> 00:18:45.040
Who here opposes?

360
00:18:46.667 --> 00:18:48.752
Why isn't he asking who agrees?

361
00:18:48.836 --> 00:18:50.462
Because it's too obvious.

362
00:18:51.839 --> 00:18:54.967
I knew it. I told you this would happen.

363
00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:56.301
Fourth item on the agenda.

364
00:18:56.385 --> 00:18:59.221
Who here opposes
repainting the buildings' exterior?

365
00:19:01.682 --> 00:19:05.936
{\an8}Next. replacing the tiles and fixing
the floor in the community center.

366
00:19:06.019 --> 00:19:06.937
Who here opposes?

367
00:19:07.521 --> 00:19:11.108
Replacing the automatic
fire detection system.

368
00:19:11.191 --> 00:19:12.151
Who opposes?

369
00:19:13.068 --> 00:19:15.821
All right. Thank you. everyone.

370
00:19:16.572 --> 00:19:20.409
Why is everyone opposed
to what Uncle says?

371
00:19:20.993 --> 00:19:23.871
Uncle Hae-kang doesn't have
his own connections there.

372
00:19:23.954 --> 00:19:25.414
That's how harsh the world is.

373
00:19:25.497 --> 00:19:26.999
People take sides

374
00:19:27.082 --> 00:19:29.585
and want their team to win
while the other loses.

375
00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:31.628
This is bad for your education.

376
00:19:32.296 --> 00:19:35.340
Then we'll wrap up True Value's
building representative meeting.

377
00:19:35.424 --> 00:19:36.258
Thank you.

378
00:19:44.558 --> 00:19:46.226
Seo Gang-won is doing a good job.

379
00:19:46.894 --> 00:19:47.728
Everyone opposed.

380
00:19:48.312 --> 00:19:52.024
Our new president
is bold enough to plant relics.

381
00:19:52.107 --> 00:19:53.817
What will he do now?

382
00:19:53.901 --> 00:19:56.069
I'm pretty sure he won't just sit back.

383
00:19:56.153 --> 00:19:56.987
Sir.

384
00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:59.698
We got a call from the head of Hansu Bank.

385
00:19:59.781 --> 00:20:00.741
Why?

386
00:20:01.241 --> 00:20:03.493
True Value's
residents' association president

387
00:20:03.577 --> 00:20:06.663
came to withdraw the entire reserve fund.

388
00:20:08.498 --> 00:20:09.625
What?

389
00:20:09.708 --> 00:20:12.711
He would've found out
that the account is empty.

390
00:20:30.187 --> 00:20:31.104
Mr. Kim.

391
00:20:31.939 --> 00:20:33.065
I get it now.

392
00:20:33.565 --> 00:20:35.859
I get why Park Hae-kang
wanted to become the president.

393
00:20:36.443 --> 00:20:37.736
What's the reason?

394
00:20:39.404 --> 00:20:41.156
The reserve fund.

395
00:20:41.240 --> 00:20:44.117
He became the president
to pocket the fund.

396
00:20:44.201 --> 00:20:47.037
I never imagined that would be the reason.

397
00:20:47.704 --> 00:20:51.375
He found out it was empty.
so he's trying to use the fund.

398
00:20:53.835 --> 00:20:55.212
I'm so excited right now.

399
00:20:55.295 --> 00:20:57.214
I'm going to lose my mind.

400
00:20:57.297 --> 00:20:59.341
I'm getting a dopamine rush!

401
00:21:05.931 --> 00:21:07.557
What's with those building reps?

402
00:21:07.641 --> 00:21:09.643
Why are they opposing everything?

403
00:21:10.602 --> 00:21:14.106
I feel like they're not helping
with the association's matters at all.

404
00:21:15.524 --> 00:21:18.110
Don't I have the authority to remove them?

405
00:21:18.193 --> 00:21:20.988
The building reps
are elected by the residents.

406
00:21:21.071 --> 00:21:24.116
so unless they're accused of corruption.
you can't dismiss them.

407
00:21:24.199 --> 00:21:26.410
They're standing in the way
of improving this place.

408
00:21:26.493 --> 00:21:27.911
That's basically corruption.

409
00:21:30.289 --> 00:21:31.123
Sir.

410
00:21:31.999 --> 00:21:33.125
Over there.

411
00:21:33.792 --> 00:21:35.419
She's our accounting manager.

412
00:21:38.797 --> 00:21:41.133
Let's say the facility manager.
the accounting manager

413
00:21:41.216 --> 00:21:44.344
and the president teamed up
and pocketed the fund.

414
00:21:44.428 --> 00:21:45.929
But even so.

415
00:21:46.013 --> 00:21:48.849
they wouldn't have emptied out
the entire account like this.

416
00:21:49.683 --> 00:21:51.018
The accounting manager.

417
00:21:51.101 --> 00:21:53.228
You didn't get to meet
since she was on vacation.

418
00:21:53.312 --> 00:21:55.397
Ha-jeong. this is the president.

419
00:21:59.443 --> 00:22:01.611
I've been wanting to meet you.

420
00:22:01.695 --> 00:22:04.031
Hello. I'm Kang Ha-jeong.

421
00:22:04.114 --> 00:22:06.992
I'm Park Hae-kang. Nice to meet you.

422
00:22:07.576 --> 00:22:08.744
Nice to meet you too.

423
00:22:10.746 --> 00:22:13.832
We'll have a lot
to discuss together from now on.

424
00:22:15.125 --> 00:22:16.335
We will?

425
00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:18.378
We can talk next time.

426
00:22:19.338 --> 00:22:20.881
I'm heading out.

427
00:22:26.511 --> 00:22:28.680
I guess our apartment complex
is changing now.

428
00:22:28.764 --> 00:22:30.932
A man who lives alone
became the president.

429
00:22:31.892 --> 00:22:33.477
He doesn't live alone.

430
00:22:34.478 --> 00:22:36.396
He has a huge family.

431
00:22:41.109 --> 00:22:42.235
Do you live alone?

432
00:22:43.028 --> 00:22:45.655
Why? Is there a problem with that?

433
00:22:47.407 --> 00:22:48.950
Was it a different guy?

434
00:22:51.703 --> 00:22:55.332
Park Hae-kang will have no choice
but to step down.

435
00:22:55.415 --> 00:22:57.584
He would have realized today

436
00:22:57.667 --> 00:22:59.628
-that he can't do whatever he wants.
-Exactly.

437
00:22:59.711 --> 00:23:03.215
He must've been feeling pretty high
and mighty about becoming the president.

438
00:23:03.298 --> 00:23:04.382
-It's so satisfying.
-Totally.

439
00:23:04.466 --> 00:23:08.512
He'll learn
that popularity doesn't mean much.

440
00:23:08.595 --> 00:23:11.932
Once Park Hae-kang steps down.
you should return to your position.

441
00:23:12.015 --> 00:23:13.016
Absolutely.

442
00:23:17.104 --> 00:23:20.482
I think that's the thing about the world.

443
00:23:23.068 --> 00:23:24.820
This is nice and sweet.

444
00:23:26.279 --> 00:23:27.823
Things tend to follow…

445
00:23:29.658 --> 00:23:32.077
their natural course.

446
00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:33.578
Of course.

447
00:23:35.539 --> 00:23:37.624
Why are they against
using the reserve fund?

448
00:23:37.707 --> 00:23:39.543
Calm down. Mr. Park.

449
00:23:40.335 --> 00:23:44.464
I'd have to be crazy
to be lying to you in this situation.

450
00:23:44.548 --> 00:23:47.134
You're giving me food. shelter
and clothes right now.

451
00:23:47.217 --> 00:23:49.386
-So?
-Gosh.

452
00:23:49.970 --> 00:23:51.638
You saw earlier

453
00:23:51.721 --> 00:23:54.599
how President Seo's supporters
are still groveling.

454
00:23:54.683 --> 00:23:59.146
That means President Seo
is still handing out kickbacks.

455
00:23:59.229 --> 00:24:00.856
-Kickbacks?
-Yeah.

456
00:24:00.939 --> 00:24:03.692
Even after Mr. Park became the president.

457
00:24:03.775 --> 00:24:06.987
those assholes
are still clinging to President Seo

458
00:24:07.070 --> 00:24:08.822
and sucking up to him.

459
00:24:08.905 --> 00:24:10.157
Why would they do that?

460
00:24:10.824 --> 00:24:14.536
Because there's still
something in it for them.

461
00:24:14.619 --> 00:24:16.454
If I ask you what that is.

462
00:24:16.538 --> 00:24:18.832
you'll just tell me
to figure it out myself.

463
00:24:21.877 --> 00:24:22.878
How did you know?

464
00:24:24.212 --> 00:24:25.714
Wanna sleep in that bag again?

465
00:24:28.049 --> 00:24:30.719
How long will you threaten me with this?

466
00:24:30.802 --> 00:24:31.970
Isn't there anything new?

467
00:24:32.053 --> 00:24:33.346
Don't take it out on me.

468
00:24:33.430 --> 00:24:35.682
You should be dealing with
President Seo's bootlickers.

469
00:24:35.765 --> 00:24:38.810
You guys look into the building reps
supporting President Seo.

470
00:24:39.477 --> 00:24:40.687
We don't have much time.

471
00:24:40.770 --> 00:24:44.441
We have to find whatever we can
and get rid of them to use the fund

472
00:24:44.524 --> 00:24:46.193
and find where it went.

473
00:24:46.276 --> 00:24:49.446
President Seo and those bootlickers…

474
00:24:49.529 --> 00:24:51.489
I'll crush them to pieces.

475
00:24:56.453 --> 00:24:58.872
Did you forget the basics
of digging into people?

476
00:25:10.300 --> 00:25:11.801
Yes. I'm heading out.

477
00:25:12.636 --> 00:25:14.679
The font is so small.

478
00:25:27.901 --> 00:25:31.154
Hey. look at the bills.
Why are you looking at food?

479
00:25:31.238 --> 00:25:33.156
I can't find anything noteworthy.

480
00:25:33.240 --> 00:25:34.866
Maybe we've lost our touch.

481
00:25:34.950 --> 00:25:36.201
I'll look through them again.

482
00:25:36.952 --> 00:25:40.163
We can't use the reserve fund
while President Seo still holds power.

483
00:25:41.456 --> 00:25:43.041
We have to take them out first.

484
00:25:46.711 --> 00:25:48.171
I'm here.

485
00:25:53.843 --> 00:25:55.637
What is all this?

486
00:25:57.889 --> 00:26:00.016
Why do you have other people's bills here?

487
00:26:05.146 --> 00:26:07.023
Why is their heating bill zero?

488
00:26:10.110 --> 00:26:11.236
This one's zero too.

489
00:26:12.279 --> 00:26:13.238
And this one?

490
00:26:13.321 --> 00:26:17.409
Wait. How can all of them be zero?

491
00:26:17.951 --> 00:26:19.035
What is it?

492
00:26:19.119 --> 00:26:20.829
What's with these houses?

493
00:26:20.912 --> 00:26:23.248
-Their heating bills are zero.
-What?

494
00:26:25.667 --> 00:26:27.794
What is it? Let me see.

495
00:26:29.337 --> 00:26:31.548
That can't be possible.

496
00:26:33.591 --> 00:26:35.051
Does this make any sense?

497
00:26:35.135 --> 00:26:36.511
Over 100 households?

498
00:26:36.594 --> 00:26:39.055
Precisely 123 households
have a heating bill of zero.

499
00:26:39.139 --> 00:26:42.475
We've checked that they're paying
for their water bills and parking.

500
00:26:42.559 --> 00:26:45.061
but it's just the heating bill
that's zero.

501
00:26:45.145 --> 00:26:47.105
These are the households
with zero heating bills.

502
00:26:47.188 --> 00:26:49.691
They're the building representatives.

503
00:26:49.774 --> 00:26:51.860
including President Seo's
closest supporters.

504
00:26:51.943 --> 00:26:56.197
There are even
former building representatives.

505
00:26:56.281 --> 00:26:58.658
Ever since President Seo
formed the association.

506
00:26:58.742 --> 00:27:02.245
he's been the president all these years.

507
00:27:03.079 --> 00:27:05.582
So all of his supporters
have zero heating bills.

508
00:27:05.665 --> 00:27:06.791
That's right.

509
00:27:06.875 --> 00:27:10.086
The accounts that wrote
malicious comments about you

510
00:27:10.170 --> 00:27:12.464
are the same as those
that have zero heating bills.

511
00:27:12.547 --> 00:27:14.299
So he even ran a troll farm.

512
00:27:15.050 --> 00:27:18.470
These guys have obviously
been doing this for a long time.

513
00:27:18.553 --> 00:27:21.681
He formed the association
about six years ago. didn't he?

514
00:27:22.682 --> 00:27:25.435
Then they could've paid
zero heating bills for six years.

515
00:27:26.227 --> 00:27:28.188
So he gave them kickbacks through this.

516
00:27:28.897 --> 00:27:32.484
But if 123 households
haven't been paying their heating fees.

517
00:27:32.567 --> 00:27:35.195
then who was paying for them?

518
00:27:35.278 --> 00:27:36.363
The other 9.000…

519
00:27:36.446 --> 00:27:40.575
So the other 9.677 households
were paying for theirs.

520
00:27:40.658 --> 00:27:41.493
That's right.

521
00:27:41.576 --> 00:27:44.954
But they won't even know
that they're paying for them.

522
00:27:45.038 --> 00:27:46.748
This is just ridiculous.

523
00:27:46.831 --> 00:27:48.833
No one found out about this for six years?

524
00:27:48.917 --> 00:27:50.627
Shouldn't we report this to the media?

525
00:27:51.211 --> 00:27:52.420
Report this?

526
00:27:53.630 --> 00:27:55.131
Yes. that's right.

527
00:27:55.215 --> 00:27:57.675
We can make them step down
as building representatives

528
00:27:57.759 --> 00:27:58.968
if we make this public.

529
00:27:59.052 --> 00:28:01.679
Right! Your brain works well
in situations like this.

530
00:28:01.763 --> 00:28:05.683
Then you could eliminate everyone
who's against you all at once.

531
00:28:07.352 --> 00:28:08.186
Yes.

532
00:28:08.269 --> 00:28:11.398
Then will you become
another Heating Bill Martyr?

533
00:28:12.273 --> 00:28:13.149
What?

534
00:28:13.233 --> 00:28:14.984
Don't you know the Heating Bill Martyr?

535
00:28:15.068 --> 00:28:18.029
The most famous martyr
besides independence fighters

536
00:28:18.113 --> 00:28:19.197
is the Heating Bill Martyr.

537
00:28:20.740 --> 00:28:22.700
Heating Bill Martyr…

538
00:28:30.458 --> 00:28:33.545
PARK HAE-KANG IS HERE
TO PROTECT YOUR HEATING BILL!

539
00:28:33.628 --> 00:28:35.672
TAKE RESPONSIBILITY
FOR HEATING BILL CORRUPTION!

540
00:28:48.268 --> 00:28:51.104
They're going totally overboard.

541
00:28:53.982 --> 00:28:56.609
{\an8}Everyone. what kind of people are we?

542
00:28:57.402 --> 00:28:59.821
We are a resilient people
who roamed the Manchurian Plains.

543
00:28:59.904 --> 00:29:01.990
spread our gallantry across the world

544
00:29:02.073 --> 00:29:05.744
and stood united
against foreign invasions and crises.

545
00:29:05.827 --> 00:29:09.372
I am standing here now with the spirit
of the independence fighters

546
00:29:09.456 --> 00:29:12.083
who gave everything to resist
during our nation's biggest crisis.

547
00:29:12.167 --> 00:29:13.251
Everyone.

548
00:29:13.334 --> 00:29:16.212
A total of 123 households

549
00:29:16.296 --> 00:29:20.884
have not paid any heating bills
for six whole years.

550
00:29:20.967 --> 00:29:22.552
I discovered this fact!

551
00:29:23.511 --> 00:29:26.222
Those 123 households
have been enjoying free heating

552
00:29:26.306 --> 00:29:28.933
thanks to someone's abuse of power.

553
00:29:29.017 --> 00:29:31.227
Zero heating bills?

554
00:29:31.311 --> 00:29:32.979
{\an8}Yes. Ms. Senior Secretary.

555
00:29:33.062 --> 00:29:36.858
I could not remain silent
in the face of such abuse of power.

556
00:29:36.941 --> 00:29:39.152
I promise to expose
all the hidden corruption

557
00:29:39.235 --> 00:29:40.820
within this apartment complex

558
00:29:41.404 --> 00:29:43.156
and fight…

559
00:29:44.949 --> 00:29:46.493
against these illegal acts!

560
00:29:48.411 --> 00:29:49.454
Everyone!

561
00:29:49.537 --> 00:29:51.623
Heating Bill Martyr!

562
00:29:53.333 --> 00:29:55.043
Problem-solver Park Hae-kang!

563
00:29:57.587 --> 00:29:59.380
Heating Bill Martyr!

564
00:30:01.049 --> 00:30:02.675
Problem-solver Park Hae-kang!

565
00:30:02.759 --> 00:30:04.052
Pay your heating bills!

566
00:30:04.135 --> 00:30:06.679
We should all pay our heating bills!

567
00:30:10.767 --> 00:30:12.602
I will solve this problem. everyone.

568
00:30:13.228 --> 00:30:16.523
<i>The former president and building reps</i>
<i>weren't paying their heating bills.</i>

569
00:30:16.606 --> 00:30:18.525
<i>Shouldn't we catch those thieves first?</i>

570
00:30:18.608 --> 00:30:20.527
<i>Those jerks took our money.</i>

571
00:30:20.610 --> 00:30:23.613
<i>All the other households</i>
<i>were paying for their heating bills.</i>

572
00:30:23.696 --> 00:30:24.948
<i>This is so unfair.</i>

573
00:30:25.031 --> 00:30:26.699
<i>This isn't mismanagement. It's fraud.</i>

574
00:30:26.783 --> 00:30:29.160
<i>Did we elect these people</i>
<i>as representatives</i>

575
00:30:29.244 --> 00:30:31.162
<i>just so they could rip us off?</i>

576
00:30:31.246 --> 00:30:33.581
<i>Don't make excuses. Take responsibility.</i>

577
00:30:33.665 --> 00:30:36.167
<i>We will not let this slide.</i>

578
00:30:37.210 --> 00:30:38.086
Wait.

579
00:30:39.003 --> 00:30:40.964
I was a mathematics major.

580
00:30:41.548 --> 00:30:44.592
Let's say the average heating bill
for a 112-square-meter house in winter

581
00:30:44.676 --> 00:30:45.844
is about 200.000 won.

582
00:30:45.927 --> 00:30:48.805
Then it'll be one million
over five months.

583
00:30:48.888 --> 00:30:50.515
and six million over six years.

584
00:30:50.598 --> 00:30:53.560
There's also hot water usage
for spring. summer. and fall.

585
00:30:53.643 --> 00:30:55.728
Then let's say it's about
ten million in total.

586
00:30:55.812 --> 00:30:57.897
But there are 123 households.

587
00:30:57.981 --> 00:30:59.524
so it's 1.23 billion.

588
00:31:00.358 --> 00:31:02.735
1.23 billion?

589
00:31:05.321 --> 00:31:09.826
<i>This shall be known as the "123 Incident."</i>

590
00:31:15.665 --> 00:31:17.250
We weren't aware of this.

591
00:31:17.333 --> 00:31:19.419
We'll be checking all 123 households.

592
00:31:19.502 --> 00:31:21.963
We can't check all the bills
for each household every month.

593
00:31:22.046 --> 00:31:23.840
Don't worry. Please just wait…

594
00:31:23.923 --> 00:31:25.383
{\an8}Yes. I'm sorry.

595
00:31:25.466 --> 00:31:26.759
{\an8}We sincerely apologize.

596
00:31:26.843 --> 00:31:28.136
{\an8}All right.

597
00:31:32.015 --> 00:31:33.308
We had no idea.

598
00:31:33.391 --> 00:31:35.435
You have to play dumb. no matter what.

599
00:31:42.567 --> 00:31:44.068
This is the management office.

600
00:31:44.152 --> 00:31:45.486
What do we do now?

601
00:31:45.570 --> 00:31:47.947
Park Hae-kang just had to meddle again.

602
00:31:48.031 --> 00:31:51.618
It seems like
he's doing everything he can to annoy us.

603
00:31:52.619 --> 00:31:55.705
We should've stopped him
from getting elected. no matter what.

604
00:31:55.788 --> 00:31:56.664
You're right.

605
00:31:56.748 --> 00:32:00.251
What do we do?
The online forum is in an uproar.

606
00:32:01.210 --> 00:32:06.174
Sir. please say something.

607
00:32:09.218 --> 00:32:10.345
Well…

608
00:32:13.097 --> 00:32:15.224
just insist that we didn't know…

609
00:32:16.476 --> 00:32:18.061
the gas meter was broken.

610
00:32:18.144 --> 00:32:20.980
What can they do if we say we didn't know?

611
00:32:23.066 --> 00:32:26.152
Would that work. though?

612
00:32:26.986 --> 00:32:30.114
Then should we just admit
that the building reps

613
00:32:30.198 --> 00:32:33.284
and some residents
who wrote comments for us

614
00:32:33.368 --> 00:32:35.286
received zero heating bills until now?

615
00:32:35.370 --> 00:32:36.788
Should I just tell the truth?

616
00:32:36.871 --> 00:32:38.414
Should we all go down together?

617
00:32:38.498 --> 00:32:41.793
You've been enjoying the benefits
for a long time.

618
00:32:41.876 --> 00:32:44.003
Use your brains…

619
00:32:44.921 --> 00:32:47.507
to think. will you?

620
00:32:47.590 --> 00:32:49.550
Just use your brains.

621
00:32:49.634 --> 00:32:51.386
Can't you think?

622
00:32:52.136 --> 00:32:56.516
Your penthouse also had zero heating bills
for the past six years.

623
00:32:57.141 --> 00:33:00.353
It seems President Seo
was overly loyal to you.

624
00:33:00.436 --> 00:33:04.148
It looks like Seo Gang-won
was busy doing something interesting.

625
00:33:04.232 --> 00:33:05.608
The other 122 households

626
00:33:05.692 --> 00:33:07.485
were close to President Seo

627
00:33:07.568 --> 00:33:09.195
or had some kind of connection.

628
00:33:10.905 --> 00:33:13.282
Gang-won is quite bold. isn't he?

629
00:33:13.366 --> 00:33:15.994
He did something
I didn't even tell him to do.

630
00:33:17.078 --> 00:33:18.913
What on earth was he thinking?

631
00:33:20.039 --> 00:33:21.207
Excuse me. sir.

632
00:33:22.583 --> 00:33:24.085
LEE SANG-GYU. GONGYEONG DAILY PRESIDENT

633
00:33:25.420 --> 00:33:28.381
-I think you should take this. sir.
-All right.

634
00:33:29.966 --> 00:33:31.968
Hello. How have you been?

635
00:33:32.051 --> 00:33:34.303
I was about to give you a call.

636
00:33:35.555 --> 00:33:37.640
You're low on fuel. aren't you?

637
00:33:38.349 --> 00:33:40.435
Why don't we fill it up?

638
00:33:43.229 --> 00:33:44.147
<i>Mr. Kim.</i>

639
00:33:44.230 --> 00:33:46.566
<i>Let's use the reserve fund.</i>

640
00:33:50.111 --> 00:33:52.655
<i>"Relics discovered at Oman New Town site…</i>

641
00:33:53.364 --> 00:33:54.949
<i>found to be fabricated.</i>

642
00:33:56.451 --> 00:33:59.871
<i>Planned by a group</i>
<i>opposing the new town project."</i>

643
00:34:00.997 --> 00:34:02.290
<i>Isn't that a nice scenario?</i>

644
00:34:03.624 --> 00:34:05.793
<i>Give him a full tank.</i>

645
00:34:06.794 --> 00:34:08.421
<i>A sedan for Gongyeong Daily…</i>

646
00:34:09.964 --> 00:34:11.841
<i>and a fruit box for the online media.</i>

647
00:34:13.843 --> 00:34:15.803
The dream of owning a home
has been delayed again.

648
00:34:15.887 --> 00:34:19.182
<i>YouTubers have a large influence</i>
<i>on public opinion these days.</i>

649
00:34:19.265 --> 00:34:20.767
<i>so let's grease some palms there too.</i>

650
00:34:20.850 --> 00:34:23.478
How will they fill
the housing supply target of 70.000 units?

651
00:34:23.561 --> 00:34:24.937
<i>Send something sweet.</i>

652
00:34:25.021 --> 00:34:28.733
{\an8}<i>So why? Who is trying</i>
<i>to stop the new town project?</i>

653
00:34:28.816 --> 00:34:30.485
<i>Planting relics at the site?</i>

654
00:34:32.195 --> 00:34:33.821
Mr. Kim.

655
00:34:33.905 --> 00:34:37.075
We spent a huge sum today. haven't we?

656
00:34:37.158 --> 00:34:40.036
I'm sure the media will move
after using all that money.

657
00:34:40.870 --> 00:34:44.373
And you spent three billion
on Hyeonpo Apartment last year.

658
00:34:44.457 --> 00:34:45.666
but there's an audit soon.

659
00:34:45.750 --> 00:34:46.709
What will you do?

660
00:34:48.753 --> 00:34:50.588
The apartment complex in Soyeong-dong.

661
00:34:50.671 --> 00:34:52.799
How much is left in that reserve fund?

662
00:34:52.882 --> 00:34:55.885
We're using that fund too.

663
00:34:55.968 --> 00:34:58.429
so there's a little over six billion left.

664
00:34:59.430 --> 00:35:01.099
I should use that then.

665
00:35:04.852 --> 00:35:06.104
You know.

666
00:35:06.813 --> 00:35:09.690
whenever I use the reserve fund
from an apartment complex.

667
00:35:11.109 --> 00:35:14.904
I feel like a kid raiding a piggy bank
without telling Dad.

668
00:35:15.905 --> 00:35:17.615
But Dad doesn't have a clue.

669
00:35:17.698 --> 00:35:19.575
Just like the residents.

670
00:35:23.121 --> 00:35:26.541
What excuse will they come up with
for not paying the heating bill?

671
00:35:26.624 --> 00:35:27.708
It's obvious.

672
00:35:27.792 --> 00:35:29.752
They'll say the gas meter was broken.

673
00:35:29.836 --> 00:35:31.212
but they had no clue.

674
00:35:31.295 --> 00:35:33.422
It's always the same excuse.

675
00:35:33.506 --> 00:35:35.133
It doesn't matter what they say.

676
00:35:35.216 --> 00:35:38.511
We just have to check
if the reserve fund is being disbursed.

677
00:35:38.594 --> 00:35:42.348
You're sure gas meter replacements
are done with the reserve fund?

678
00:35:42.431 --> 00:35:44.642
Yes. It's different
for every apartment complex.

679
00:35:44.725 --> 00:35:46.769
but. fortunately.
it's stated in the regulations.

680
00:35:46.853 --> 00:35:49.021
-You'd better be sure.
-I am.

681
00:35:49.605 --> 00:35:52.859
And we can use this chance to wipe out

682
00:35:53.526 --> 00:35:56.529
President Seo's faction in one go.

683
00:36:01.617 --> 00:36:03.452
{\an8}TRUE VALUE STATE
123 INCIDENT HEARING

684
00:36:03.536 --> 00:36:05.288
{\an8}Do you think we're running a charity?

685
00:36:05.371 --> 00:36:06.789
This should be front-page news!

686
00:36:06.873 --> 00:36:09.000
I just can't believe this!

687
00:36:09.876 --> 00:36:11.669
How could you do this to all of us?

688
00:36:14.964 --> 00:36:16.591
I will step down

689
00:36:17.175 --> 00:36:19.343
and return to being an ordinary resident

690
00:36:19.427 --> 00:36:21.262
of True Value--

691
00:36:21.345 --> 00:36:23.055
Are you kidding me?

692
00:36:23.139 --> 00:36:25.808
Stepping down won't solve anything!

693
00:36:25.892 --> 00:36:28.311
You think that will make it okay?

694
00:36:28.394 --> 00:36:32.148
We need to report this to the police.

695
00:36:32.732 --> 00:36:34.734
We need to request an audit

696
00:36:34.817 --> 00:36:38.112
and figure out exactly what happened.

697
00:36:38.196 --> 00:36:40.907
down to every last detail.

698
00:36:40.990 --> 00:36:41.824
Don't you agree?

699
00:36:41.908 --> 00:36:43.743
-You're right!
-Yes!

700
00:36:45.286 --> 00:36:46.537
I mean…

701
00:36:46.621 --> 00:36:50.082
Honestly. I don't get
why you're blaming everything on us.

702
00:36:50.166 --> 00:36:51.959
Our gas meters were broken.

703
00:36:52.043 --> 00:36:54.086
What were we supposed to do?

704
00:36:54.170 --> 00:36:57.506
Do you all just stare
at your gas meters every day?

705
00:36:58.507 --> 00:37:01.219
Even if you didn't see your gas meter.

706
00:37:01.302 --> 00:37:03.721
you would've seen your bill.

707
00:37:03.804 --> 00:37:06.974
You had zero heating bills
in the middle of winter.

708
00:37:07.058 --> 00:37:09.977
How could you not know
for six whole years?

709
00:37:10.061 --> 00:37:11.479
Six years!

710
00:37:12.104 --> 00:37:15.191
Do you hear what he's saying?
He's supposed to be a building rep!

711
00:37:15.274 --> 00:37:18.444
-Ridiculous.
-Building reps are people too!

712
00:37:18.527 --> 00:37:21.864
Sometimes we're too busy
to check our bills.

713
00:37:21.948 --> 00:37:24.742
I set up automatic payments.
so I don't check them sometimes.

714
00:37:24.825 --> 00:37:25.743
Automatic payments?

715
00:37:25.826 --> 00:37:27.328
Are we not people too?

716
00:37:27.411 --> 00:37:29.789
Are you kidding me? "Automatic payments"?

717
00:37:29.872 --> 00:37:31.707
This is just nonsense. Hey.

718
00:37:31.791 --> 00:37:35.253
Even so. this is strange.

719
00:37:35.336 --> 00:37:39.548
Why did this happen
only to the building representatives?

720
00:37:39.632 --> 00:37:41.634
That's exactly what I mean.

721
00:37:41.717 --> 00:37:45.263
And we mothers really can't understand
how the facility manager

722
00:37:45.346 --> 00:37:47.390
didn't know about this for six years.

723
00:37:47.473 --> 00:37:49.809
It's your job to oversee this. Mr. Choi.

724
00:37:49.892 --> 00:37:51.811
Mr. Choi. come over here.

725
00:37:51.894 --> 00:37:53.813
Say something. Come over here.

726
00:37:53.896 --> 00:37:57.233
-Tell us.
-Just tell us everything.

727
00:37:57.316 --> 00:37:58.567
What happened?

728
00:37:58.651 --> 00:38:00.611
Just explain everything.

729
00:38:03.823 --> 00:38:05.658
I…

730
00:38:10.121 --> 00:38:10.955
Well…

731
00:38:11.038 --> 00:38:12.540
This is infuriating.

732
00:38:13.291 --> 00:38:15.918
I have nothing to say.

733
00:38:16.002 --> 00:38:17.378
I'm really sorry.

734
00:38:19.130 --> 00:38:21.799
Mr. Choi. I'm disappointed in you.

735
00:38:21.882 --> 00:38:23.551
I had no idea he was that kind of person.

736
00:38:23.634 --> 00:38:24.510
Unbelievable.

737
00:38:25.886 --> 00:38:28.097
Calm down. everyone!

738
00:38:28.180 --> 00:38:29.932
I understand how you feel.

739
00:38:30.016 --> 00:38:33.936
but this has already happened.
so we must figure out how to resolve this.

740
00:38:34.020 --> 00:38:36.022
The most urgent matter

741
00:38:36.105 --> 00:38:38.524
is to replace the broken gas meters.

742
00:38:39.191 --> 00:38:40.818
-With the reserve fund--
-But…

743
00:38:40.901 --> 00:38:41.777
Yes?

744
00:38:41.861 --> 00:38:43.988
Why would you use
the reserve fund for that?

745
00:38:45.740 --> 00:38:47.241
The management regulations

746
00:38:47.325 --> 00:38:50.661
state that gas meter replacements
should be done with the reserve fund.

747
00:38:50.745 --> 00:38:54.457
So I'll take care of that issue
according to the regulations.

748
00:38:56.292 --> 00:38:58.294
Is there something you'd like to say?

749
00:39:00.755 --> 00:39:04.050
I live on the top floor of Building 123.

750
00:39:04.133 --> 00:39:07.386
It turns out that
I had zero heating bills as well.

751
00:39:08.179 --> 00:39:09.597
I wasn't aware.

752
00:39:09.680 --> 00:39:14.185
I don't check the gas meter or my bills.

753
00:39:14.268 --> 00:39:18.189
I know it may sound irresponsible
to say I didn't know.

754
00:39:18.939 --> 00:39:22.401
but I agree with
what the building reps are saying.

755
00:39:25.654 --> 00:39:28.449
There was something going on with him too.

756
00:39:28.532 --> 00:39:29.742
That is why

757
00:39:30.326 --> 00:39:32.244
I will pay for all the heating bills

758
00:39:32.328 --> 00:39:34.830
I haven't paid for until now.

759
00:39:35.998 --> 00:39:38.459
Wouldn't it only be right
for all the building reps

760
00:39:39.043 --> 00:39:40.419
to do the same?

761
00:39:41.045 --> 00:39:42.129
Wait.

762
00:39:42.213 --> 00:39:44.715
This wasn't our fault.

763
00:39:44.799 --> 00:39:46.842
Why should we pay for everything--

764
00:39:46.926 --> 00:39:49.678
Well. you've found out now.
so you should pay your bills.

765
00:39:50.262 --> 00:39:52.056
The heating bills that you haven't paid

766
00:39:52.139 --> 00:39:55.226
have been paid
by all the other residents so far.

767
00:39:55.810 --> 00:39:59.063
You should at least be feeling sorry.

768
00:39:59.146 --> 00:40:00.439
We're all neighbors.

769
00:40:00.523 --> 00:40:02.566
-He's right.
-Right.

770
00:40:02.650 --> 00:40:03.484
Everyone.

771
00:40:03.567 --> 00:40:06.278
The man living in the penthouse
really is different.

772
00:40:06.362 --> 00:40:08.989
They say generosity comes from money.

773
00:40:09.073 --> 00:40:11.325
but he also seems to have a conscience.

774
00:40:11.409 --> 00:40:13.119
That's very admirable.

775
00:40:14.703 --> 00:40:15.830
You're so cool.

776
00:40:15.913 --> 00:40:17.456
-You're cool!
-Very admirable.

777
00:40:21.085 --> 00:40:22.128
Mr. Seo.

778
00:40:25.005 --> 00:40:26.382
What do you think?

779
00:40:28.759 --> 00:40:30.219
Me? I…

780
00:40:31.512 --> 00:40:32.471
Mr. Seo.

781
00:40:41.188 --> 00:40:42.356
Well. I…

782
00:40:43.399 --> 00:40:45.276
Since you asked for my opinion.

783
00:40:45.359 --> 00:40:49.321
I also believe we should pay
for all the heating bills.

784
00:40:49.405 --> 00:40:51.157
-President Seo.
-President Seo.

785
00:40:51.240 --> 00:40:52.741
What are you saying?

786
00:40:54.827 --> 00:40:55.911
Of course.

787
00:40:55.995 --> 00:40:58.038
Of course. they should pay their bills.

788
00:40:58.539 --> 00:41:00.374
All right. That's great.

789
00:41:00.875 --> 00:41:02.126
Then now.

790
00:41:02.668 --> 00:41:05.171
I'll recheck all the households
that had zero heating bills

791
00:41:05.254 --> 00:41:07.798
and collect all the fees
that they haven't paid.

792
00:41:07.882 --> 00:41:09.967
And I'll make sure

793
00:41:10.050 --> 00:41:13.721
to distribute the collected fees
to the remaining 9.677 households

794
00:41:13.804 --> 00:41:16.599
who have had to pay extra until now.

795
00:41:18.100 --> 00:41:19.185
You're amazing!

796
00:41:19.268 --> 00:41:20.352
We love you!

797
00:41:32.531 --> 00:41:33.824
President Park.

798
00:41:41.540 --> 00:41:44.335
You seemed as wise as King Solomon today.

799
00:41:44.418 --> 00:41:46.462
"Recover the unjust gains

800
00:41:46.545 --> 00:41:49.715
and distribute them equally
to the people."

801
00:41:51.509 --> 00:41:53.177
That was so cool.

802
00:41:53.260 --> 00:41:55.513
I was more impressed by your words.

803
00:41:55.596 --> 00:41:57.056
In any case. thank you.

804
00:41:57.640 --> 00:42:00.267
Keep up the good work. President Park.

805
00:42:03.437 --> 00:42:04.313
Bye.

806
00:42:04.396 --> 00:42:06.232
-Thank you.
-Bye.

807
00:42:06.315 --> 00:42:08.609
I was curious what kind of people
lived in penthouses.

808
00:42:08.692 --> 00:42:09.693
Mr. Lee?

809
00:42:09.777 --> 00:42:12.488
He's very humble and cool.
unlike many rich people.

810
00:42:12.571 --> 00:42:14.281
-You know him?
-When did you start admiring him?

811
00:42:14.365 --> 00:42:15.491
Since the moment we saw him.

812
00:42:15.574 --> 00:42:17.243
Anyone rich is admirable.

813
00:42:17.326 --> 00:42:19.662
Great job. President Park.

814
00:42:19.745 --> 00:42:21.580
-Thank you.
-We're rooting for you.

815
00:42:21.664 --> 00:42:22.498
Thank you.

816
00:42:22.581 --> 00:42:24.708
Goodbye.

817
00:42:28.837 --> 00:42:31.549
You did a decent job today.

818
00:42:32.132 --> 00:42:33.259
But…

819
00:42:33.968 --> 00:42:35.970
don't let your guard down.

820
00:42:36.053 --> 00:42:39.890
I'm keeping an eye on you.

821
00:42:41.809 --> 00:42:44.103
Good job today. guys. See you later.

822
00:42:44.186 --> 00:42:45.688
-Bye.
-Bye. Ms. Senior Secretary.

823
00:42:45.771 --> 00:42:46.897
{\an8}Get home safely. ma'am.

824
00:42:47.481 --> 00:42:48.983
You should lose some weight.

825
00:42:50.317 --> 00:42:51.151
Mr. Kim.

826
00:42:51.819 --> 00:42:53.612
Have you seen <i>Spider-Man?</i>

827
00:42:54.488 --> 00:42:56.865
Yes. a long time ago.

828
00:43:02.288 --> 00:43:05.040
"With great power
comes great responsibility."

829
00:43:05.124 --> 00:43:06.041
The famous quote?

830
00:43:06.834 --> 00:43:08.502
Yes.

831
00:43:09.044 --> 00:43:11.297
It's time for Seo Gang-won

832
00:43:11.380 --> 00:43:13.757
to take responsibility.

833
00:43:14.258 --> 00:43:17.511
I gave him power over 9.800 households.

834
00:43:18.345 --> 00:43:21.056
but he gave birth
to a heating bill martyr.

835
00:43:22.600 --> 00:43:25.394
Will you invite Gang-won
on a date with me?

836
00:43:26.395 --> 00:43:27.229
Yes. sir.

837
00:43:33.861 --> 00:43:35.321
Were you all notified?

838
00:43:35.821 --> 00:43:37.615
-About the 123 Incident heating bills?
-Yes.

839
00:43:38.198 --> 00:43:41.744
We'll each get an equal share
of the fees paid by the 123 households.

840
00:43:42.828 --> 00:43:46.665
I heard they'll deduct that amount
from this month's maintenance fee.

841
00:43:46.749 --> 00:43:49.668
I should pay more attention
to my maintenance bill from now on.

842
00:43:49.752 --> 00:43:50.711
Me too.

843
00:43:50.794 --> 00:43:53.672
I never paid attention
since it's paid from my husband's account.

844
00:43:54.173 --> 00:43:55.257
In any case.

845
00:43:55.799 --> 00:43:58.594
isn't our president
really good at his job?

846
00:43:58.677 --> 00:44:00.471
He's handsome. and he's so capable.

847
00:44:00.554 --> 00:44:01.388
I know. right?

848
00:44:01.472 --> 00:44:04.808
These days. I've been watching
all the residents' association meetings.

849
00:44:04.892 --> 00:44:06.393
It's like I'm watching a celebrity.

850
00:44:07.394 --> 00:44:09.521
He does seem a bit different.

851
00:44:09.605 --> 00:44:13.108
I can sense his passion.

852
00:44:13.192 --> 00:44:16.403
What he did regarding the heating bills
was pretty touching.

853
00:44:16.487 --> 00:44:21.408
The way he exposed the 123 Incident
and even resolved the issue…

854
00:44:21.909 --> 00:44:24.578
I feel so relieved
that our residents' association president

855
00:44:24.662 --> 00:44:25.871
is someone like him.

856
00:44:26.455 --> 00:44:28.165
-True.
-You're right.

857
00:44:28.248 --> 00:44:30.000
Totally. I'm so happy.

858
00:44:30.084 --> 00:44:31.418
Yes!

859
00:44:31.502 --> 00:44:32.961
Let's have beer next time.

860
00:44:33.045 --> 00:44:34.463
How about some beer?

861
00:44:38.509 --> 00:44:40.969
{\an8}PRESIDENT PARK HAE-KANG

862
00:44:46.850 --> 00:44:47.685
Yes?

863
00:44:53.065 --> 00:44:54.817
You're here. Ms. Senior Secretary.

864
00:44:57.277 --> 00:44:58.529
Come and sit down.

865
00:45:12.543 --> 00:45:15.337
You said you needed a week.

866
00:45:15.421 --> 00:45:16.630
Was that…

867
00:45:17.256 --> 00:45:20.217
so you could take care
of the 123 Incident?

868
00:45:21.718 --> 00:45:23.470
It was an urgent matter.

869
00:45:31.186 --> 00:45:34.356
I already have so much to do.

870
00:45:35.023 --> 00:45:37.109
That you do.

871
00:45:38.235 --> 00:45:39.069
But…

872
00:45:40.070 --> 00:45:42.531
would a week be enough. President Park?

873
00:45:43.866 --> 00:45:44.700
What?

874
00:45:48.412 --> 00:45:50.038
Goodbye. Ms. Senior Secretary.

875
00:46:04.052 --> 00:46:07.723
With great power
comes great responsibility.

876
00:46:10.601 --> 00:46:11.685
Sir.

877
00:46:15.981 --> 00:46:16.815
Yes?

878
00:46:17.649 --> 00:46:19.318
It's me. sir.

879
00:46:19.401 --> 00:46:22.905
I know you must be busy.

880
00:46:23.530 --> 00:46:26.450
but I wanted to ask
when I should come pick up the money.

881
00:46:27.451 --> 00:46:29.453
Come in two hours.

882
00:46:30.037 --> 00:46:30.871
All right.

883
00:46:47.930 --> 00:46:50.140
{\an8}This is premium Italian hardwood flooring.

884
00:46:51.350 --> 00:46:53.477
They said it was resistant to cracking.

885
00:46:54.436 --> 00:46:56.146
Mr. Kim. I think it's cracked.

886
00:46:58.273 --> 00:47:01.527
It seems like you hit the floor
a little too hard with the golf club.

887
00:47:01.610 --> 00:47:03.529
But it doesn't really show.

888
00:47:05.989 --> 00:47:07.157
Really?

889
00:47:09.284 --> 00:47:10.869
Damn it.

890
00:47:12.621 --> 00:47:17.459
My 300-million-won floor
almost got ruined because of you.

891
00:47:18.085 --> 00:47:19.169
Can't you hear me?

892
00:47:22.881 --> 00:47:23.715
{\an8}Seo Gang-won.

893
00:47:24.341 --> 00:47:25.175
Seo Gang-won.

894
00:47:25.759 --> 00:47:27.719
Wake up. Seo Gang-won!

895
00:47:27.803 --> 00:47:31.098
Seo Gang-won!

896
00:47:36.395 --> 00:47:38.313
You can't just die like this.

897
00:47:40.107 --> 00:47:42.025
Don't you know how much I lost?

898
00:47:42.109 --> 00:47:44.403
You should've served your purpose
until the end.

899
00:47:45.612 --> 00:47:47.364
-Mr. Kim.
-Yes. sir.

900
00:47:48.282 --> 00:47:49.992
We should move him

901
00:47:51.034 --> 00:47:53.078
to Taegowon.

902
00:48:00.919 --> 00:48:02.045
Be careful.

903
00:48:12.806 --> 00:48:14.683
{\an8}TAEGOWON

904
00:48:18.520 --> 00:48:20.147
All right!

905
00:48:32.534 --> 00:48:33.952
Thinking back on it.

906
00:48:34.036 --> 00:48:37.289
you really didn't have anything to offer.

907
00:48:37.998 --> 00:48:40.751
You weren't capable.
and you weren't even funny either.

908
00:48:41.335 --> 00:48:43.170
So why don't you

909
00:48:43.253 --> 00:48:45.130
become fertilizer for this mountain…

910
00:48:46.465 --> 00:48:49.301
and take good care…

911
00:48:50.927 --> 00:48:52.220
of our baby trees now?

912
00:49:03.815 --> 00:49:05.484
Take good care of them.

913
00:49:27.130 --> 00:49:30.133
Where the hell is he going?

914
00:49:30.967 --> 00:49:32.427
Something's fishy.

915
00:49:56.910 --> 00:49:57.911
He's going inside.

916
00:50:13.802 --> 00:50:15.220
-Did you take it?
-Yes.

917
00:50:19.057 --> 00:50:20.976
"Tae…" What is it?

918
00:50:21.560 --> 00:50:22.644
"Taegowon."

919
00:50:22.728 --> 00:50:24.104
-Taegowon?
-Yes.

920
00:50:24.187 --> 00:50:25.605
What is this place?

921
00:50:34.614 --> 00:50:37.868
SEO GANG-WON

922
00:50:39.870 --> 00:50:40.996
Hello.

923
00:50:42.080 --> 00:50:44.040
You arrived just in time.

924
00:50:44.124 --> 00:50:44.958
Yes. sir.

925
00:50:45.584 --> 00:50:47.711
-Mr. Kim. give him the money.
-Yes. sir.

926
00:50:54.092 --> 00:50:55.510
I don't get

927
00:50:56.219 --> 00:50:57.554
how Park Hae-kang found out.

928
00:50:58.388 --> 00:51:00.098
-I'm sorry. sir.
-No. it's fine.

929
00:51:00.724 --> 00:51:02.350
It was quite amusing.

930
00:51:02.434 --> 00:51:05.061
I swear I won't let it happen again--

931
00:51:05.145 --> 00:51:06.354
Don't.

932
00:51:07.689 --> 00:51:08.523
Pardon?

933
00:51:09.524 --> 00:51:10.901
I'm enjoying this.

934
00:51:12.068 --> 00:51:14.613
so just let Park Hae-kang
do what he wants.

935
00:51:16.531 --> 00:51:17.991
Yes. sir.

936
00:51:19.409 --> 00:51:22.704
Since you're here.
you should pay your respects.

937
00:51:24.915 --> 00:51:25.791
All right.

938
00:51:27.042 --> 00:51:28.084
Here.

939
00:51:33.381 --> 00:51:35.383
{\an8}Former President Seo Gang-won's…

940
00:51:36.760 --> 00:51:37.761
{\an8}tree.

941
00:51:39.971 --> 00:51:44.351
This is the tree that will grow
with Seo Gang-won's flesh and blood.

942
00:51:48.188 --> 00:51:50.482
Let's pay our respects.

943
00:51:53.193 --> 00:51:55.111
May you live a long life.

944
00:52:13.922 --> 00:52:14.840
He's back.

945
00:52:14.923 --> 00:52:16.216
Take photos.

946
00:52:20.637 --> 00:52:21.721
That's a bag of cash.

947
00:52:22.556 --> 00:52:23.640
Cash?

948
00:52:30.480 --> 00:52:31.439
Taegowon?

949
00:52:31.523 --> 00:52:33.400
The facility manager tripped.

950
00:52:33.483 --> 00:52:36.361
and that bag was filled
with 50.000 won bills.

951
00:52:36.862 --> 00:52:39.030
Did any other employees
do anything suspicious?

952
00:52:39.114 --> 00:52:42.158
Besides the facility manager.
everyone else is working late.

953
00:52:42.242 --> 00:52:44.327
And they're replacing
the gas meters tomorrow?

954
00:52:44.411 --> 00:52:45.787
Yes. sir.

955
00:52:45.871 --> 00:52:48.790
Then the facility manager
must have gotten the money for that.

956
00:52:49.374 --> 00:52:51.501
I did a search.
and Taegowon is a tree farm.

957
00:52:51.585 --> 00:52:54.254
They mostly sell trees
used for apartment landscaping.

958
00:52:55.297 --> 00:52:57.007
A tree farm?

959
00:53:04.723 --> 00:53:06.558
TAESAN PARK
TAESAN CONSTRUCTION. TAESAN PLANT…

960
00:53:08.059 --> 00:53:09.394
TS NETWORKS

961
00:53:09.477 --> 00:53:11.521
<i>Taegowon is owned by TS Networks.</i>

962
00:53:11.605 --> 00:53:13.440
It's a real estate development company.

963
00:53:13.523 --> 00:53:15.609
one of Taesan Construction's affiliates.

964
00:53:15.692 --> 00:53:17.068
And TS Networks

965
00:53:17.152 --> 00:53:19.154
is True Value's developer.

966
00:53:19.237 --> 00:53:21.364
while Taesan Construction
is the construction company.

967
00:53:21.448 --> 00:53:22.782
TAESAN CONSTRUCTION

968
00:53:22.866 --> 00:53:25.660
<i>That means Taesan is behind all this.</i>

969
00:53:26.244 --> 00:53:27.412
Would they even see us?

970
00:53:31.082 --> 00:53:31.917
Boss.

971
00:53:32.000 --> 00:53:32.834
Huh?

972
00:53:32.918 --> 00:53:35.378
Places like this won't see you
without an appointment.

973
00:53:36.254 --> 00:53:37.297
Just let me give it a try.

974
00:53:40.425 --> 00:53:41.343
Hello.

975
00:53:42.802 --> 00:53:44.638
Please inform the president
that True Value's

976
00:53:44.721 --> 00:53:47.140
residents' association president
is here to see them.

977
00:53:47.223 --> 00:53:48.683
He's waiting for you. sir.

978
00:53:49.267 --> 00:53:51.061
-What?
-Please follow me.

979
00:53:52.896 --> 00:53:54.272
It wasn't me.

980
00:54:01.321 --> 00:54:05.325
…46. 47. 48. 49. 50. 51. 52.

981
00:54:05.408 --> 00:54:07.035
That's 52 points.

982
00:54:07.118 --> 00:54:09.829
with <i>pibak. gwangbak. meongtta.</i>

983
00:54:09.913 --> 00:54:11.581
a shake. a three-go and a four-go.

984
00:54:11.665 --> 00:54:13.541
so it'll be 342.800 won.

985
00:54:15.543 --> 00:54:19.089
If someone's winning over 300.000 won
in a 100-won-a-point game.

986
00:54:19.172 --> 00:54:21.299
it's no longer just a game.
That's gambling.

987
00:54:21.383 --> 00:54:23.385
Have you been visiting gambling dens?

988
00:54:24.177 --> 00:54:27.555
Go-Stop is all about momentum.

989
00:54:29.724 --> 00:54:30.850
Momentum.

990
00:54:30.934 --> 00:54:31.935
Come on.

991
00:54:32.644 --> 00:54:35.855
Even if we're a fake family.
I'm still your father-in-law.

992
00:54:36.356 --> 00:54:37.273
Ha-ri.

993
00:54:37.357 --> 00:54:39.442
At least give me a discount.

994
00:54:42.779 --> 00:54:44.614
Hang on. Hello?

995
00:54:44.698 --> 00:54:47.993
Hello. I'm Gyeong-buk's teacher
from the Stanford Class.

996
00:54:48.952 --> 00:54:51.830
Gyeong-buk seems to have a bit of a fever.

997
00:54:51.913 --> 00:54:54.249
What? Gyeong-buk has a fever?

998
00:54:55.458 --> 00:54:57.460
Please make sure everything goes smoothly.

999
00:54:57.544 --> 00:54:58.878
All right.

1000
00:55:00.130 --> 00:55:03.758
The gas meter replacements
will be done by today.

1001
00:55:04.676 --> 00:55:06.011
Great work. everyone.

1002
00:55:06.094 --> 00:55:08.346
We're not getting
any more calls from the residents.

1003
00:55:08.430 --> 00:55:10.348
We can finally get some rest.

1004
00:55:11.016 --> 00:55:13.601
Everyone's happy that
their maintenance fees will be reduced

1005
00:55:13.685 --> 00:55:15.270
with the recovered heating charges.

1006
00:55:15.353 --> 00:55:18.398
Why don't we have lunch together
to celebrate?

1007
00:55:18.481 --> 00:55:19.441
Yes!

1008
00:55:19.524 --> 00:55:22.360
We can recharge
and get our spirits back up.

1009
00:55:22.986 --> 00:55:25.196
Sure. Everyone worked hard.

1010
00:55:25.780 --> 00:55:27.657
It's lunchtime. Let's go.

1011
00:55:27.741 --> 00:55:29.868
-Yes. sir.
-Awesome.

1012
00:55:30.410 --> 00:55:32.078
Aren't you joining us. Ms. Kang?

1013
00:55:32.704 --> 00:55:34.164
I'm not feeling well.

1014
00:55:34.247 --> 00:55:35.832
Come with us. Ha-jeong.

1015
00:55:35.915 --> 00:55:37.792
You worked the hardest.

1016
00:55:37.876 --> 00:55:39.169
Come on.

1017
00:55:47.469 --> 00:55:48.928
-Come on. you scared me.
-Hey.

1018
00:55:49.763 --> 00:55:51.389
-Don't eat that.
-Sorry.

1019
00:55:51.473 --> 00:55:54.392
Boss. she said
the president was waiting for us.

1020
00:55:54.476 --> 00:55:55.894
Isn't that strange?

1021
00:55:55.977 --> 00:55:57.812
Maybe we were being followed.

1022
00:55:57.896 --> 00:56:00.565
It feels like they set a trap.
knowing we were coming.

1023
00:56:06.237 --> 00:56:08.031
What took you so long. President Park?

1024
00:56:08.114 --> 00:56:10.533
I've been waiting for you all this time.

1025
00:56:12.869 --> 00:56:14.120
Come inside.

1026
00:56:14.204 --> 00:56:16.498
Let us talk. president to president.

1027
00:56:16.581 --> 00:56:19.250
Come on. Watch your step.

1028
00:56:19.334 --> 00:56:20.210
Boss…

1029
00:56:21.002 --> 00:56:24.464
PHARMACY

1030
00:56:25.090 --> 00:56:26.549
Are you sure you're okay?

1031
00:56:27.050 --> 00:56:27.926
Yes.

1032
00:56:28.551 --> 00:56:29.385
Let's go.

1033
00:56:30.762 --> 00:56:32.889
This isn't something to say
to a kindergartener.

1034
00:56:32.972 --> 00:56:35.141
but you should take care of your own body.

1035
00:56:35.225 --> 00:56:37.018
Being sick only hurts yourself.

1036
00:56:37.102 --> 00:56:40.355
No one can suffer in your place.
Not your dad or your uncles.

1037
00:56:40.438 --> 00:56:41.439
Okay.

1038
00:56:42.023 --> 00:56:43.149
Mom…

1039
00:56:43.233 --> 00:56:45.610
I mean. Ha-ri.

1040
00:56:47.070 --> 00:56:49.697
Can't you carry my bag today?

1041
00:56:51.116 --> 00:56:51.950
No.

1042
00:56:52.534 --> 00:56:55.787
People are meant to carry
the burdens assigned to them.

1043
00:56:55.870 --> 00:56:57.413
We all have to carry our own cross.

1044
00:56:57.497 --> 00:56:59.624
That's the weight of life.

1045
00:57:00.375 --> 00:57:02.544
My friends' moms

1046
00:57:02.627 --> 00:57:06.756
always carry their bags
as soon as they come pick them up.

1047
00:57:16.099 --> 00:57:17.475
There. Happy?

1048
00:57:18.101 --> 00:57:19.853
Ma'am.

1049
00:57:19.936 --> 00:57:21.729
-Hello.
-Hello.

1050
00:57:22.313 --> 00:57:23.273
Is someone sick?

1051
00:57:23.773 --> 00:57:25.859
Oh. your kid's sick.

1052
00:57:25.942 --> 00:57:27.277
-Oh. dear.
-Hello.

1053
00:57:27.360 --> 00:57:29.988
Do you have a fever?
I hope you get better soon.

1054
00:57:30.488 --> 00:57:34.409
Ma'am. President Park
didn't come to work today.

1055
00:57:34.492 --> 00:57:36.453
Do you know where he went?

1056
00:57:37.537 --> 00:57:39.706
-Well…
-Hello. ma'am.

1057
00:57:39.789 --> 00:57:41.875
-Hello.
-Hello.

1058
00:57:42.375 --> 00:57:43.626
-We'll get going.
-Sure.

1059
00:57:43.710 --> 00:57:45.044
-Bye.
-Bye.

1060
00:57:45.128 --> 00:57:46.796
-Get well soon.
-Bye.

1061
00:57:46.880 --> 00:57:47.881
Bye.

1062
00:58:00.602 --> 00:58:01.478
Ha-jeong.

1063
00:58:04.397 --> 00:58:06.941
This is my office. Come here.

1064
00:58:08.026 --> 00:58:09.402
You know.

1065
00:58:09.486 --> 00:58:12.363
I was so shocked by your performance.

1066
00:58:12.447 --> 00:58:14.491
I have so many questions.

1067
00:58:14.574 --> 00:58:17.118
How did you find out
about the heating bills?

1068
00:58:17.952 --> 00:58:19.662
Right. You found the relics too.

1069
00:58:19.746 --> 00:58:21.623
Are you just good at finding stuff?

1070
00:58:22.332 --> 00:58:24.083
But those relics were authentic.

1071
00:58:24.709 --> 00:58:26.503
Where did you get those from?

1072
00:58:27.086 --> 00:58:28.546
It must have cost a fortune.

1073
00:58:30.507 --> 00:58:31.382
Right.

1074
00:58:31.466 --> 00:58:34.427
I prepared a small gift for you. Mr. Park.

1075
00:58:34.511 --> 00:58:36.137
Do you want to see? Come on.

1076
00:58:37.430 --> 00:58:38.306
Here.

1077
00:58:39.474 --> 00:58:40.433
Come on.

1078
00:58:50.318 --> 00:58:51.277
Ta-da.

1079
00:58:52.904 --> 00:58:55.114
It was hard choosing which photo to frame

1080
00:58:55.198 --> 00:58:57.534
since you looked good
in every one of them.

1081
00:58:58.117 --> 00:58:59.077
Do you like it?

1082
00:59:01.246 --> 00:59:03.790
But I don't like it.

1083
00:59:03.873 --> 00:59:07.085
I should've gotten a clear shot
of the disappointed look on your face

1084
00:59:07.168 --> 00:59:10.088
when you heard the bank balance.

1085
00:59:11.422 --> 00:59:14.092
<i>He knows everything.</i>

1086
00:59:16.386 --> 00:59:17.220
Are you really…

1087
00:59:18.012 --> 00:59:19.889
the president of Taesan Construction?

1088
00:59:21.891 --> 00:59:22.850
Right.

1089
00:59:23.768 --> 00:59:25.562
I haven't introduced myself properly.

1090
00:59:27.564 --> 00:59:29.566
I'm the president of Taesan Construction.

1091
00:59:30.441 --> 00:59:31.651
Lee Chung-won.

1092
00:59:34.571 --> 00:59:37.031
I'm Lee Chung-won from Building 123.

1093
00:59:37.615 --> 00:59:38.533
<i>We'll…</i>

1094
00:59:40.660 --> 00:59:42.787
be seeing each other again.

1095
00:59:55.925 --> 00:59:58.177
You seem to be great at finding things.

1096
00:59:58.261 --> 01:00:00.555
so what are you looking for here
at Taesan Group?

1097
01:00:01.347 --> 01:00:04.434
Whatever it is. I'm afraid
you won't be able to find it here.

1098
01:00:05.018 --> 01:00:06.477
I feel sorry about that.

1099
01:00:08.438 --> 01:00:10.565
No. I've already found it.

1100
01:00:14.319 --> 01:00:15.236
Why don't you…

1101
01:00:16.821 --> 01:00:19.699
let me become your right-hand man?

1102
01:00:26.497 --> 01:00:29.417
THE APARTMENT JOB

1103
01:00:53.524 --> 01:00:56.861
{\an8}<i>I'll do whatever it takes to support you.</i>

1104
01:00:56.944 --> 01:00:58.905
{\an8}<i>Ha-jeong. just go live your own life.</i>

1105
01:00:58.988 --> 01:01:01.032
{\an8}Ms. Kang. were you crying?

1106
01:01:01.115 --> 01:01:03.034
{\an8}<i>Mr. Park. please let me stay the night.</i>

1107
01:01:03.618 --> 01:01:05.244
{\an8}A love story?

1108
01:01:05.328 --> 01:01:07.622
{\an8}<i>President Seo was the keeper of my vault.</i>

1109
01:01:07.705 --> 01:01:10.041
{\an8}<i>I'm going to become</i>
<i>Lee Chung-won's vault keeper.</i>

1110
01:01:10.124 --> 01:01:12.251
{\an8}<i>-Let's go meet President Seo first.</i>
-President Seo?

1111
01:01:12.335 --> 01:01:14.587
{\an8}<i>-He went on a trip abroad?</i>
<i>-I don't know.</i>

1112
01:01:14.671 --> 01:01:15.922
{\an8}<i>He betrayed us.</i>

1113
01:01:16.005 --> 01:01:18.257
{\an8}<i>Release Yong-man on medical bail first.</i>

1114
01:01:18.341 --> 01:01:19.884
{\an8}Bring the cash. then we'll talk.

1115
01:01:19.967 --> 01:01:22.762
{\an8}<i>It seems Chief Son</i>
<i>is holding Park Yong-man hostage.</i>

1116
01:01:22.845 --> 01:01:25.223
{\an8}<i>So that's why Park Hae-kang</i>
<i>needed the money.</i>

1117
01:01:25.306 --> 01:01:27.725
{\an8}<i>Boss. becoming Lee Chung-won's</i>
<i>vault keeper is dangerous.</i>

1118
01:01:27.809 --> 01:01:29.185
{\an8}<i>Do you trust Park Hae-kang?</i>

1119
01:01:29.268 --> 01:01:32.605
{\an8}<i>I'm going to put him to the test.</i>

1120
01:01:36.734 --> 01:01:38.736
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park
